# quality.jsonl — claims graded 0..1 by the judge against `must`, the points a complete answer covers.
# `source` is the page each rubric was written from; every point was read on that page.
# Schema: {"id","claim","must":[ "point", ... ],"source":"<repo-relative page>"}
{"id":"qual-01","claim":"What happens when I run `cckit effort start` on a new effort while the WIP limit is already reached, and how do I start anyway?","must":["the start is refused once the efforts in progress are at the limit, which defaults to 2","in progress means an effort/<N>-<slug> branch exists as a local head or on origin","a refused start creates no branch, no worktree and no board change","--force or KIT_FORCE=1 starts anyway","re-running start on an effort that is already in progress is always allowed"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/effort-reference.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-02","claim":"How does `cckit qa up` decide that a lane is usable, and what does each of its exit codes mean?","must":["a lane is usable only when every qa.readiness probe answers in the same polling round","a 2xx or 3xx answer counts as up; 4xx, 5xx and connection refused do not","exit 0: the lane is usable","exit 1: the wait timed out or the stack command exited first","exit 2: refused before anything launched, for example no qa.command or a lane port already in use","exit 3: jq or curl is missing"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/qa-reference.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-03","claim":"What does `cckit hotfix` do with a merged PR, step by step, and what happens on a conflict?","must":["a digits-only argument is a PR number, and an unmerged PR is refused","it creates a worktree on branch fix/<N>-hotfix-<base> cut from origin/<base>, main unless --base names another","it picks with git cherry-pick -x, adding -m 1 for a merge commit","it opens a PR against that base titled after the source, with 'Cherry-pick of #N' in the body and no Closes line","on a conflict nothing is pushed: resolve it in the worktree, run git cherry-pick --continue, then run the same cckit hotfix again"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/ship/releasing.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-04","claim":"Who can write a night grant that night mode will honour, and which floors can no grant waive?","must":["the grant is a comment carrying the night-grant marker on the plan parent issue","it counts only when GitHub reports the author as OWNER, or the author is github.owner or a login in night.grantors","a marker comment from any other author is ignored","the floors workflows, cost and secret can never be waived, plus any listed in night.neverWaivable","each waiver must equal one floor name; a wildcard or several names in one string is refused"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/config-and-permissions.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-05","claim":"When does a session claim written by `cckit start` end?","must":["nothing has to release it","it is dropped when its session pid is dead, or alive with a different start time because the pid was reused","it is dropped when its worktree has been gone for more than five minutes","a claim written on another host is never dropped on a pid check","--force or KIT_FORCE=1 on a later start takes the claim over"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/development/many-sessions.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-06","claim":"What does `cckit init --upgrade` never touch in a project?","must":["a rule, skill, agent, script or instruction file that already exists is preserved, edited or not","a hook the project customized is kept and reported as Drifted","a path listed under upgrade.removed, or a key of upgrade.renamed, is skipped and never re-added","a config value the project set is kept over the template's","a feature block the config does not have is not added"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/getting-started/update.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-07","claim":"How does `cckit orchestrate --results` classify the way each worker ended, and what are its exit codes?","must":["success: the agent process exited 0","failure: it exited 1 to 128","interrupted: it died on a signal, or its record still says running and its pid is gone","untracked: Herdr started the agent, so cckit has no exit status","it exits 0 when every worker succeeded, 1 when any failed or was interrupted or there are no records, and 3 when none failed but some are unfinished"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/wave-reference.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-08","claim":"Which two limits does instruction-budget-lint hold, and what are the two ways to bring the resident total down?","must":["the resident total, CLAUDE.md files plus every rule without paths: frontmatter, is limited to 150000 bytes","any one instruction file is limited to 200 lines","it is a ratchet: an offender recorded in the baseline may stay but not grow","scope a rule to one surface by giving it a paths: list in its frontmatter","split it: keep a short rule resident and move the reference material to a knowledge doc"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/review/gates.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-09","claim":"How does an optional integration get switched on and installed, and what does my consent cover?","must":["cckit add <id> sets the integration's one config key and installs nothing","cckit doctor installs a missing tool only after a yes at its prompt, or with --fix","with no terminal and no --fix the doctor installs nothing, reports the tool missing and exits 1","the yes is recorded as an install:<id> line in .cckit/consent","that line permits installing that one integration in that one repo, and KIT_ASSUME_YES is not consent"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/integrations.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-10","claim":"Why is a pull request that GitHub reports as mergeable not necessarily safe to merge, and what has to happen first?","must":["mergeable only means no textual conflict: a branch cut from a base that has since moved can revert a sibling's change with no conflict and no failing check","bring the branch onto the current base, by fetching and rebasing onto origin/<base>, and pass the gate there before merging","read the diff against the base for a deletion the issue never asked for","cckit watch --merge rebases nothing: a BEHIND pull request is classified BLOCKED and skipped","GitHub reports BEHIND only when the base branch's protection requires branches to be up to date"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/rules.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-11","claim":"What does a Codex-only `cckit init` write into a project, compared with a Claude Code one?","must":["the instruction file is AGENTS.md, not CLAUDE.md","skills and rules go under .agents/, not .claude/","hooks go under .codex/hooks/ and are registered in .codex/hooks.json","the config is cckit.config.json at the repository root and the manifest is .cckit/kit.manifest.json, with no .claude/ directory","the memory hooks, the statusline and the settings files are not installed"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/install-matrix.mdx"}
{"id":"qual-12","claim":"Which limits does `cckit autopilot run` enforce in code, and which are partly enforced or unsupported?","must":["--max-iters (default 5) and the wall-clock limits --max-seconds and --round-seconds (defaults 3600 and 900) are enforced","a round that changes neither HEAD nor the working tree stops the run","--max-tokens is checked only between rounds, so one round can overshoot the ceiling","a cost limit is unsupported, and --notify is refused because nothing delivers a notification","a run never merges and never closes an issue"],"source":"docs-site/src/content/docs/agent-compatibility.mdx"}
